{
  "abstract": "A Mathlib-only formalization of two explicit three-action improper phi-regret families in Section 4.4.1 of Dann, Mansour, Mohri, Schneider, and Sivan (COLT 2025). They are finite counterexample families for the paper's rate-preserving linear-reduction program. It proves valid-improper certificates, the affine-hyperplane invariant-transport core of Lemma 4, the extreme-point antipodal-displacement core of Lemma 5, a direct finite one-way affine action/loss-transfer-to-canonical bridge, a source-style two-direction affine linear-equivalence-to-canonical bridge in an explicit bijective-coordinate regime, finite-dimensional Equation-(15)-to-(16) and Equation-(16)-to-(17) bridges, and concrete Equation-(18) vertex/corner criteria. These mechanisms rule out the selected canonical, normalized, finite-loss-basis, homogeneous/affine-transfer, two-direction affine-equivalence, and finite-vertex/corner proper reductions for the two cited families.",
